 in the required domain.\n\nThe general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x-\\frac{\\pi }{4} & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}+n\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the equation above for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\frac{\\pi }{4}+n\\pi  \\\\ 3x & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi  \\\\ x & =\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{n\\pi }{3} \\\\ x & =\\frac{(2n+1)\\pi }{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe set $n=0,\\pm 1,\\pm 2,…,$ until we have generated all solutions in the domain $0\\le x<\\pi .$\n\n- Setting $n=0$ gives $x=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$\n\n- Setting $n=1$ gives $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$\n\n- Setting $n=2$ gives $x=\\frac{5\\pi }{6}$\n\nAll other values of $n$ generate solutions outside the domain $0\\le x<\\pi .$ So, the solutions ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3},{x}_{4}$ (written in ascending order) are\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{\\pi }{6},\\,\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\,\\frac{5\\pi }{6}\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${x}_{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and ${x}_{3}=\\frac{5\\pi }{6},$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}=\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\cdot \\frac{5\\pi }{6}=\\frac{5{\\pi }^{2}}{12}.\n$$" 13194139534333 true] [17592186283635 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283636 13194139534333 true] [17592186283635 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283637 13194139534333 true] [17592186283635 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283638 13194139534333 true] [17592186283635 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283639 13194139534333 true] [17592186283635 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283640 13194139534333 true] [17592186283635 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534333 true] [17592186283635 1041 "selection" 13194139534333 true] [17592186283635 1104 #edb/ref 17592186283636 13194139534333 true] [17592186283635 1110 #uuid "72684fcf-8a1d-562b-a067-4c43bb6e8957" 13194139534333 true] [17592186283636 1034 "\\frac{5{\\pi }^{2}}{12}" 13194139534333 true] [17592186283636 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534333 true] [17592186283636 1111 #uuid "4744d360-e084-557e-9788-b79051b0a470" 13194139534333 true] [17592186283637 1034 "\\frac{5\\pi }{6}" 13194139534333 true] [17592186283637 1103 